# Build context exclusions for the agent image ONLY.
#
# Honoured by BuildKit, which looks for a file named `<dockerfile-path>.dockerignore`
# and uses it INSTEAD of the root `.dockerignore`. The classic builder falls back to
# the root file, which is why the root file is a floor and never excludes a path any
# Dockerfile COPYs.
#
# What this context must contain, and why:
#
#   agent/requirements.txt   agent/Dockerfile line 22, via
#                            `ARG PYTHON_DEPS=agent/requirements.txt`. Copied before
#                            the application source so that editing application code
#                            does not invalidate the dependency layer.
#   agent/                  agent/Dockerfile line 40, `COPY --chown=10001:10001`.
#
# Everything else is dead weight in the upload, and this is where that is expressed.
# The root `.dockerignore` deliberately cannot exclude `internal/` or `cmd/`, because
# cmd/sentinel/Dockerfile COPYs both — which is exactly why this per-image file is
# required rather than decorative. It is what lets the agent build stay lean while
# the Sentinel build stays correct.
#
# Consequence worth stating: the root `.dockerignore` is still consulted for a
# classic-builder agent build, and it no longer excludes these paths either, so both
# builders now produce the same image content for a given set of source changes.

# The Go Sentinel is a separate image with a separate build. Nothing in the Python
# agent reaches into it, and its test files import Go packages only via the Go test
# harness.
cmd/
internal/

# Not needed at runtime by either the app or its test suite. The agent's own tests
# live in agent/tests/ and are inside the copied `agent/` tree, so excluding the
# repository-root `tests/` does not remove them.
tests/
deploy/
docs/
scripts/
.opencode/

# Documentation and governance files.
*.md

# Belt and braces on the virtualenv: the root file already excludes `.venv*/`, and
# this repeats it so the agent context stays lean even if a future edit to the root
# file relaxes that pattern for an unrelated image.
.venv*/
**/.venv*/

# Local scratch that a developer may have left in the worktree.
tmpdump/
